01:13:21.143 --> 01:13:30.163
[SPEAKER_01]: It was time. So we climbed up there. It was an amazing climb. When we reached the top at 8 p.m., it was a little bit too windy, but we knew it's

01:13:30.243 --> 01:13:40.386
[SPEAKER_01]: midnight sun, we can wait. Around 11 p.m., the wind calmed down. Everything was just red and orange. By the midnight sun, shortly before

01:13:40.486 --> 01:13:50.449
[SPEAKER_01]: midnight, we took off from the top of Mount Stettin. This is just an unforgettable experience. I feel you, man. Chasing golden apple from

01:13:50.509 --> 01:14:01.028
[SPEAKER_00]: above is quite mystical. I'm not going to deny that. A chasing golden hour with the Norwegian backdrop. I'll let people imagine that

01:14:01.089 --> 01:14:08.774
[SPEAKER_00]: themselves. It's quite out of the world. I think on that note, Andreas, before we wrap up, there was a super cool thing you had on your website,

01:14:08.954 --> 01:14:17.319
